"We are looking for an experienced and proactive Operations Manager to help DOAJ operate effectively and sustainably.&nbsp; Working closely with the Managing Director and colleagues across the organisation, you will help develop the systems, processes and ways of working that enable DOAJ to deliver its mission.&nbsp;

As a small, globally distributed organisation, DOAJ relies on effective coordination across teams. The Operations Manager plays an important role in ensuring that information flows effectively, processes are clear, and colleagues have the support they need to deliver their work.

This role would suit someone who enjoys improving services, managing information and processes, and supporting a mission-driven organisation. We welcome applications from people with experience in operations, libraries, information management, scholarly communication, research support, publishing, nonprofit organisations or related fields."

By Hannah Hillen

DOI: https://doi.org/10.70950/rtnk6247

&nbsp;

We have a wonderful reason to celebrate—Thoth Open Metadata has been named a finalist for the 2026 ALPSP Award for Innovation in Publishing! Following our shortlist nomination in late June and a presentation early July to the judging panel by our COO, Toby Steiner, we are incredibly proud to see our community-led platform recognised on this international stage.

This achievement brings our team back to Manchester from 9-11th September 2026, for the annual ALPSP Conference at The Manchester Deansgate Hotel. We are excited to deliver an in-person, lightning showcase during the Awards Finalists session

